  "body": "## Problem\n\nThe GPU parity tests (`crates/gpu/tests/cut_onto.rs`, `cut_parity.rs` and others) skip by name when there is no adapter. The gate runs them without `--nocapture`, so the SKIP line is hidden. The post-merge workflow sets no `CAMCRAFT_REQUIRE_GPU`. On a Linux runner with no adapter, the parity tests therefore count as a pass, and nobody sees that they did not run.\n\nFound by the review of PR #3878 (#2629, slice S3a). On the review machine, the shared device chose the software adapter WARP, not the Intel Arc.\n\n## Fix\n\n- The gate counts a named GPU skip and prints it in the step summary (\"SKIPPED (no adapter): <test>\"). \"Not run\" is never a pass (AGENTS.md).\n- The step report names the adapter that the tests used (hardware or software).\n- Decide, and record in `docs/decisions/`, if the post-merge runner sets `CAMCRAFT_REQUIRE_GPU` (it has a GPU) or stays at \"skip, but report\".\n\n## Notes\n\n- Follow-up from the review of PR #3878.\n",
